@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `law08-vintage`
IMPORT `law08-nouns`

-- Chuong III, Muc 4-5 (Dieu 87-93): developing and offering insurance products and the methods of calculating
-- premium (Dieu 87, amended by Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(7)), State-supported products, reinsurance and
-- co-insurance, outsourcing, and the transfer of portfolios of contracts.

§ `Chuong III, Muc 4: Hoat dong nghiep vu`

§§ `Dieu 87: developing, designing and offering insurance products`

@@q 1757 1759
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1757-1759)
`Dieu 87(1) — insurers and foreign non-life branches are free and answerable for their own product development (statement; no rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "The insurer takes the initiative and answers for building, designing and developing its products."

-- Dieu 87(2): rules, terms and rates must satisfy four requirements.
@@q 1760 1775
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1760-1775)
GIVEN r IS A `Rules, terms and rates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 87(2): the rules, terms and rates meet the requirements` r MEANS
        r's `comply with the law and fit Vietnamese practice, ethics, culture and custom`
    AND r's `the language of the rules and terms is accurate, simple and easy to understand and technical terms are defined`
    AND r's `state clearly insurable interest, object, scope and risks, the rights and duties of the policyholder and insured person, the insurer's liability, exclusions, the method of paying and the dispute provisions`
    AND r's `premium is built on statistics, corresponds to the conditions and liability and ensures solvency`

-- Dieu 87(3) and (3a). V1: an insurer must register, and the Ministry of Finance must approve, the premium
-- method of life, health and motor vehicle products, except compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle
-- owners. From V2 (Law 139/2025/QH15 Dieu 1(7)(a)): registration and approval for life and health products only;
-- for motor vehicle products (again except compulsory civil liability) a non-life insurer or foreign non-life
-- branch gives the Ministry written notice before applying or changing the method and must keep to the notified
-- method. The premium of compulsory civil liability insurance is fixed by the Government under Dieu 8(5), not here.
-- A product line the article does not name has no such requirement (the freedom of Dieu 87(1)) (fork F28).
@@q 1776 1782
@@qa 165 178
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1776-1782; src:law139-2025-qh15:165-178)
GIVEN m IS A `A premium method`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` m MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the rules in force are those of V2 or later`
           THEN CONSIDER m's `product line`
                WHEN `a life insurance product`    THEN m's `registered with the Ministry of Finance` AND m's `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance`
                WHEN `a health insurance product`  THEN m's `registered with the Ministry of Finance` AND m's `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance`
                WHEN `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product`
                     THEN m's `notified in writing to the Ministry of Finance before it was applied or changed` AND m's `the insurer applies the method it notified`
                WHEN `compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners`
                     THEN REFUSE "the premium of compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners is fixed under Dieu 8(5); Dieu 87(3) and (3a) exclude it"
                WHEN `another non-life insurance product` THEN TRUE
           IF `the rules in force are those of V1 or later`
           THEN CONSIDER m's `product line`
                WHEN `a life insurance product`    THEN m's `registered with the Ministry of Finance` AND m's `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance`
                WHEN `a health insurance product`  THEN m's `registered with the Ministry of Finance` AND m's `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance`
                WHEN `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product` THEN m's `registered with the Ministry of Finance` AND m's `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance`
                WHEN `compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners`
                     THEN REFUSE "the premium of compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners is fixed under Dieu 8(5); Dieu 87(3) excludes it"
                WHEN `another non-life insurance product` THEN TRUE
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "Law 08/2022/QH15 was not in force before 1 January 2023"

-- Dieu 87(4): the ways an insurer may offer products.
@@q 1783 1789
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1783-1789)
GIVETH A LIST OF `A way of supplying insurance products`
`Dieu 87(4): the ways an insurer may offer products` MEANS
    LIST `directly`, `through an insurance agent or broker`, `through a tender`, `through an electronic transaction`, `another way the law allows`

-- Dieu 87(5)-(6): the Government details the registration procedure, the Minister of Finance details the
-- premium methods and the supply of products. V1 refers to khoan 3; V2 to khoan 3 and 3a.
@@q 1790 1794
@@qa 180 185
@ref Dieu 87 (src:1790-1794; src:law139-2025-qh15:180-185)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 87(5): the Government's rules on the dossier, order and procedure to register or notify a premium method` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 87(5) delegates the dossier, order and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 87(6): the Minister of Finance's rules on premium methods and on supplying products` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 87(6) delegates the premium methods and the supply of products to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 88: products the State supports`

@@q 1796 1815
@ref Dieu 88 (src:1796-1815)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 88(2): the Government's rules on the measures supporting agricultural, forestry, fishery and social-security products` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 88(2) delegates the detail of the support measures to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"

`Dieu 88(1) — the State may support these products by one or more of seven measures: simpler procedures, publicity, risk funds, data and technology, distribution channels, a part of the premium from the budget, inter-ministry cooperation (a list of State measures; no private rule evaluated)` MEANS
    "Measures (a) to (g), chosen by the State."

§§ `Dieu 89: reinsurance, ceding, co-insurance, the motor vehicle insurance fund, risk funds`

@@q 1820 1828
@ref Dieu 89 (src:1820-1828)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 89(1): the foreign reinsurer meets the credit rating and the other conditions the Government sets` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 89(1) requires a credit rating from international rating agencies and other conditions set by the Government; neither is among the sources"

-- Dieu 89(2). Insurers and foreign non-life branches may co-insure, if both are licensed under this Law.
@@q 1829 1837
@ref Dieu 89 (src:1829-1837)
GIVEN c IS A `A would-be co-insurer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 89(2): the enterprise may take part in co-insurance` c MEANS
    c's `is an insurer or a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` AND c's `holds a licence to establish and operate under this Law`

@@q 1838 1853
@ref Dieu 89 (src:1838-1853)
`Dieu 89(3)-(4) — the motor vehicle insurance fund is made of contributions of non-life insurers selling compulsory motor vehicle liability insurance and is managed centrally; insurers may agree to form risk funds (descriptions of funds; the management is the Government's: Dieu 89(3) last sentence, 89(4))` MEANS
    "The fund and the risk funds are described, not regulated, by these paragraphs."

@@q 1854 1855
@ref Dieu 89 (src:1854-1855)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 89(5): the Minister of Finance's rules on reinsurance, ceding and co-insurance` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 89(5) delegates the detail to the Minister of Finance; the Minister's circular is not among the sources"

§§ `Dieu 90: outsourcing`

-- Dieu 90(1). Four activities cannot be outsourced.
@@q 1857 1865
@ref Dieu 90 (src:1857-1865)
GIVEN o IS AN `An outsourcing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 90(1): the activity may be outsourced` o MEANS
    NOT (   o's `the outsourced activity is internal control`
         OR o's `the outsourced activity is internal audit`
         OR o's `the outsourced activity is risk management`
         OR o's `the outsourced activity is advising on, introducing or offering insurance products or arranging the making of insurance contracts`)

-- Dieu 90(2)(dd). The provider must perform at least 75% of the value of the work itself; if part is
-- subcontracted, the insurer's prior written consent is needed.
@@q 1892 1899
@ref Dieu 90 (src:1892-1899)
GIVEN o IS AN `An outsourcing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 90(2)(dd): the provider and any subcontracting meet the Law's requirements` o MEANS
        o's `share of the value of the work the provider performs itself` AT LEAST 75%
    AND (   NOT o's `part of the work is subcontracted`
         OR o's `the insurer consented to the subcontract in writing in advance`)

-- Dieu 90(3). The outsourcing contract is in writing and has ten essential contents.
@@q 1902 1925
@ref Dieu 90 (src:1902-1925)
GIVEN o IS AN `An outsourcing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 90(3): the outsourcing contract is in the form and has the contents the Law requires` o MEANS
        o's `the outsourcing contract is in writing`
    AND o's `the contract states scope and content`
    AND o's `the contract states time and place`
    AND o's `the contract states the rights and obligations of both sides`
    AND o's `the contract states quality standards and requirements`
    AND o's `the contract states the provider's duty to give information and report`
    AND o's `the contract states the contingency, remedy and compensation if the provider cannot or does not perform`
    AND o's `the contract states the mechanism to supervise, control and audit, and separate accounting`
    AND o's `the contract restricts subcontracting`
    AND o's `the contract states the mechanism to keep data and customer information confidential`
    AND o's `the contract states the way of resolving disputes`

§ `Chuong III, Muc 5: Chuyen giao danh muc hop dong bao hiem`

§§ `Dieu 91: when a portfolio is transferred`

@@q 1932 1942
@ref Dieu 91 (src:1932-1942)
GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 91: the transfer of the portfolio is one of the cases the Law lists` t MEANS
        t's `the Ministry of Finance required it under Dieu 113(8)(c) or (d)`
    OR  t's `it narrows the content or scope of activity`
    OR  t's `it follows a division, split, merger, consolidation, dissolution or cessation`
    OR  t's `it follows a revocation under Dieu 75(1)(a), (d) or (e)`

§§ `Dieu 92: conditions for transferring a portfolio`

@@q 1944 1949
@ref Dieu 92 (src:1944-1949)
GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 92(1): the receiving insurer meets the conditions` t MEANS
        t's `the receiving insurer is already carrying on the line transferred`
    AND t's `the receiving insurer meets the capital adequacy ratio and solvency requirements`
    AND t's `the receiving insurer meets the conditions to run the line after receipt`

-- Dieu 92(2): assets corresponding to the technical reserve of the whole portfolio go with it.
@@q 1950 1952
@ref Dieu 92 (src:1950-1952)
GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 92(2): the assets transferred correspond to the technical reserve` t MEANS
    t's `value of the assets transferred` AT LEAST t's `technical reserve of the whole portfolio transferred`

-- Dieu 92(3). Rights and duties under the contracts do not change until the contracts end; but in a Dieu 91(1)
-- transfer, if the assets are below the reserve, the receiver must agree with the policyholders a reduction of
-- the sum insured or benefits. The Law gives no formula for the reduction: only the duty to negotiate arises.
@@q 1953 1960
@ref Dieu 92 (src:1953-1960)
GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 92(3): the receiving insurer must agree a reduction of sums insured or benefits with the policyholders` t MEANS
    t's `the Ministry of Finance required it under Dieu 113(8)(c) or (d)` AND t's `value of the assets transferred` BELOW t's `technical reserve of the whole portfolio transferred`

@@q 1961 1962
@ref Dieu 92 (src:1961-1962)
`Dieu 92(4) — a policyholder who does not agree to the transfer may terminate unilaterally (the consequence is Dieu 26(4), 27(4); see law08-ch2-general.l4)` MEANS
    "The policyholder's right to terminate."

§§ `Dieu 93: procedure for transferring a portfolio`

-- Dieu 93(1)-(2). A written request to the Ministry of Finance with the reasons, plan and contract; the transfer
-- goes ahead only after the Ministry's written approval; within 30 days of the approval the transferor publishes
-- on its website and notifies the policyholders in writing.
@@q 1964 1977
@ref Dieu 93 (src:1964-1977)
GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 93(1): the transfer may go ahead` t MEANS
    t's `the Ministry of Finance approved in writing`

GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A DATE
`Dieu 93(2): the last day to publish and notify the policyholders` t MEANS
    t's `date the Ministry of Finance approved` PLUS 30

GIVEN t IS A `A portfolio transfer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 93(2): the publication and notice were in time` t MEANS
    t's `date the transferor published and notified the policyholders` AT MOST `Dieu 93(2): the last day to publish and notify the policyholders` t

@@q 1978 1979
@ref Dieu 93 (src:1978-1979)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Dieu 93(3): the Government's rules on the dossier, order and procedure of transferring a portfolio` MEANS
    REFUSE "Dieu 93(3) delegates the dossier, order and procedure to the Government; its decree is not among the sources"
